## The slice

The pack generates one vertical slice and no example business features:

- `app/sign-in/page.tsx` is the page labelled "Local development sign-in".
- `app/api/session/route.ts` signs in (`POST`) and out (`DELETE`). Sign-in asks the backend's local development identity (`POST /api/dev-identity/token` of `shared/api-contracts/openapi.yml`) for a token and keeps it in an httpOnly cookie. Neither handler returns the token.
- `app/page.tsx` shows `GET /api/me`, read through the generated client in `lib/api/client.ts`.
- `lib/auth/session.ts` holds the cookie name (`{{ app_id | replace('-', '_') }}_session`) and options.
- `lib/app-info.ts` holds the display name and the audience. The audience is display text only: no route, check or permission reads it.
- `tests/` holds the Vitest unit and component tests of all of the above.

## The dev identity is not authentication

The sign-in is a local development identity. The backend serves it only under its `local` profile and to loopback requests, so a deployed backend answers 404 and the sign-in fails closed. Never present it as complete authentication, and do not ship it. The real identity provider, the authorization policy and the secrets are the project's own: replace the sign-in with the provider before anything ships (the `security-auth` and `web-conventions` skills describe how).

## Build & Run

- **Install**: `npm ci` (the lockfile is committed; `package.json` and the lockfile read their versions from `packs/versions.yml` of the Prism template)
- **Run**: `npm run dev` (port {{ port }}, listening on 127.0.0.1 only; `.env.development` turns on the local development sign-in, which a production build never offers); copy `.env.example` to `.env.local` first. `API_BASE_URL` is the only variable and defaults to `http://localhost:8080`
- **Test**: `npm test` (Vitest with Testing Library; unit and component tests with a mocked backend)
- **Lint / typecheck / build**: `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`
- **API client**: `npm run generate:api` regenerates `lib/api/generated/schema.d.ts` from `shared/api-contracts/openapi.yml`; every other script runs it first, and git ignores the output
- The root `Taskfile.yml` wraps these as `task {{ app_id }}:dev`, `:test`, `:lint`, `:typecheck`, `:build` and `:generate-api`

## Critical Rules

### Forbidden Patterns

- Calling the backend from the browser, or putting the token in `localStorage`, a response body or a client component
- Hand-written fetches to contract paths: add the operation to the OpenAPI contract and call it through the generated client
- Reading `audience` anywhere but the display text
- Secrets or tokens in the repository

### Gotchas

- Apps on `localhost` share one cookie jar whatever their port, so each app has its own cookie name; keep it unique when you rename an app.
- The profile page and the sign-in route handler are dynamic. Test a server page by awaiting it and rendering the result, as `tests/profile-page.test.tsx` does.
- Do not move a dependency to another major version of its pinned baseline by hand: the pins live in `packs/versions.yml` and the lockfile follows them.

## Architecture

```
{{ app_path }}/
  app/            - App Router: pages, layout, the session route handler
  components/     - the sign-in form, the sign-out button and the profile card
  lib/api/        - the contract client (`client.ts`), its base URL (`config.ts`) and the generated types
  lib/auth/       - the session cookie
  lib/app-info.ts - display name and audience
  tests/          - Vitest tests
```

